  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Gattermann – Koch reaction is used for the industrial production of benzaldehyde. </p><p>In Gattermann – Koch reaction, benzene is treated with carbon monoxide in the acidic medium in presence of anhydrous aluminium chloride to give benzaldehyde. In this reaction, anhydrous aluminium chloride works as a catalyst. It is an electrophilic substitution reaction.<img src=\"assets\\st0039_9a118541f91e.png\" style=\"width: 600px; height: 183px;\"/></p>"
